Here is my analysis of the owner capacity/city-limit feature.

## Summary

The city capacity feature has two distinct pieces that are worth calling out because they don't fully line up:
1. A **hard 50-owner-per-city limit** that is fully implemented (rejects creation with 409).
2. A **`capacityWarning` field** that is asserted by an acceptance test but is **NOT implemented anywhere in production code** (no field, no DTO property, no mapping). This is the most important finding.

## 1. The hard "50 owners per city" limit

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/validation/CityOwnerLimitException.java`
- `public class CityOwnerLimitException extends RuntimeException` (line 23)
- `public static final long MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY = 50;` (line 26)
- `public static final String FIELD = "city";` (line 29)
- Constructor `CityOwnerLimitException(String city)` builds message "City already contains the maximum of 50 owners: <city>" (lines 31-33)

Related sibling for the daily cap: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/validation/DailyOwnerLimitException.java` — `MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY = 100`, `FIELD = "registrationDate"`.

## 2. Owner entity, DTO, service, controller

- **Entity/model:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` — `@Entity @Table(name = "owners")`. Note it has `private Boolean bulkSignupWarning;` (line 88, column `bulk_signup_warning`) with getter/setter (lines 245-251). There is **no `capacityWarning` field**.
- **DTO / response class:** generated from OpenAPI spec `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml`. The `OwnerDto` schema defines `bulkSignupWarning` (openapi.yml line 2222-2229) but **no `capacityWarning` property**. (`OwnerDto.java` is code-generated at build time; not present in source tree.)
- **Mapper:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` — `@Mapper` interface, `OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner)` (line 46) with many `@Mapping` expressions. No mapping for `capacityWarning`.
- **Service layer:** 
  - Interface `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicService.java` — `long countOwnersByCity(String city)` (line 67).
  - Impl `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java` — `countOwnersByCity` (lines 275-279) delegates to `ownerRepository.countByCity(city)`; also `countOwnersByRegistrationDate` (lines 281-285).
